              "c": "老師",
              "j": "lou5 si1",
              "e": "teacher"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "family-t1-s03",
          "c": "我有一個哥哥。",
          "j": "ngo5 jau5 jat1 go3 go4 go1.",
          "e": "I have one older brother.",
          "note": "Cantonese names siblings by age, not just gender — 哥哥 (go4 go1) \"older brother\", 弟弟 (dai6 dai2) \"younger brother\", 姐姐 (ze4 ze1) \"older sister\", 妹妹 (mui4 mui2) \"younger sister\". There's no single word for just \"brother\"; you must pick older or younger.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "我",
              "j": "ngo5",
              "e": "I"
            },
            {
              "c": "有",
              "j": "jau5",
              "e": "have"
            },
            {
              "c": "一個",
              "j": "jat1 go3",
              "e": "one (person)"
            },
            {
              "c": "哥哥",
              "j": "go4 go1",
              "e": "older brother"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "family-t1-s04",
          "c": "妹妹好細個。",
          "j": "mui4 mui2 hou2 sai3 go3.",
          "e": "Younger sister is very young.",
          "note": "細 (sai3) is the Cantonese \"small\" (Mandarin 小 siu2), and 細個 (sai3 go3) means \"young / little\" of a person — 好細個 (hou2 sai3 go3) \"very young\". Its opposite is 大 (daai6) \"big / grown / older\".",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "妹妹",
              "j": "mui4 mui2",
              "e": "younger sister"
            },
            {
              "c": "好",
              "j": "hou2",
              "e": "very"
            },
            {
              "c": "細個",
              "j": "sai3 go3",
              "e": "young / small"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "family-t1-s05",
          "c": "爺爺住喺香港。",
          "j": "je4 je2 zyu6 hai2 hoeng1 gong2.",
          "e": "Grandfather lives in Hong Kong.",
          "note": "Grandparents split by side of the family: 爺爺 (je4 je2) and 嫲嫲 (maa4 maa2) are your father's parents; 公公 (gung1 gung1) / 婆婆 (po4 po4) — or 外公 (ngoi6 gung1) / 外婆 (ngoi6 po4) — are your mother's. 住喺 (zyu6 hai2) is \"live at\".",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "爺爺",
              "j": "je4 je2",
              "e": "paternal grandfather"
            },
            {
              "c": "住",
              "j": "zyu6",
              "e": "lives"
            },
            {
              "c": "喺",
              "j": "hai2",
              "e": "in / at"
            },
            {
              "c": "香港",
              "j": "hoeng1 gong2",
              "e": "Hong Kong"
            }
          ]
        }
